Cached `profile` in a local pointer and used `__builtin_expect` to keep the valid path as the fall-through, letting the compiler emit a single predictable branch and fewer redundant loads on the hot path.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p == NULL, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (__builtin_expect(idx >= p->numFields, 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[idx].num;
}
```